  "suggestion": "Remove the oppressive scanline overlay to let the pixel art breathe and pop; use a subtle CRT curvature or chromatic aberration instead for atmosphere. Replace the gray button with a high-contrast, pixel-art styled button (e.g., bright red or yellow with a chunky 3D border) that pulses or animates. Swap the title font for a custom, jagged pixel font that matches the game's aesthetic. Increase the saturation of the sky and snow to create a more vibrant, energetic mood. Integrate the UI into the world—perhaps the skier is standing on the 'START' text or the instructions are written on a pixelated signpost."
}

